    "title": "Added a bootable portfolio desktop",
    "body": "## Session\n\n- **Area:** Three.js interaction design, canvas interfaces, raycasting, camera movement, accessibility, testing, and deployment\n- **Goal:** Make the computer screen behave as one powered-off object before revealing its usable desktop files.\n\n## Work completed\n\n- Preserved the previous scene on `backup/pre-powered-desktop-v16-2026-07-31`.\n- Changed the monitor from an always-on set of file targets into one full-screen power target.\n- Added a short AFFAN_OS boot sequence with staged progress, monitor texture updates, and PC power-light feedback.\n- Added a dedicated camera move that frames the monitor as a readable desktop.\n- Kept the Archtech, SSIK, About, Inspiration, Contact, and Resume targets disabled until boot completes.\n- Added a visible desktop exit control, Escape-to-overview support, and a screen-reader power control.\n- Added regression checks for the new power target, boot state, and desktop controls.\n- Updated the project README, pushed the source to GitHub, and deployed the verified build to Cloudflare.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Live site: <https://affan-shaikh-portfolio.sil6428-archtech.workers.dev>\n- Source: <https://github.com/sil6428/Portfolio.github.io>\n- Portfolio commit: `13a3546`\n- Cloudflare version: `b8d44c3d-e129-4528-9e09-5b3d242f159b`\n- Checks: `npm run lint` and `npm test`\n\n## What I learned\n\n- One large raycast surface gives a powered-off monitor a clear interaction before smaller desktop targets become relevant.\n- Separating visual state from hit-test state prevents invisible file targets from intercepting the first screen click.\n- A CanvasTexture supports off, booting, and ready states without replacing the Three.js monitor model.\n- A close camera angle still needs an explicit exit path and keyboard-accessible equivalent.\n\n## Next step\n\n- Gather feedback on the desktop camera distance and the timing of the boot sequence.\n- Test the powered-on file targets on a lower-powered touch device.\n\n## Commit check\n\n- [x] This entry describes real work completed today.\n- [x] Every placeholder has been replaced or removed.\n- [x] No credentials, secrets, or private personal data are included."
